    <!-- ============ SECTION 3: READING ============ -->
    <section id="reading">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="tag">03</span><h2>Reading</h2></div>
      <p class="sec-sub">Read the passage, then answer the questions that follow.</p>

      <div class="passage">
        <h3>Starting Over</h3>
        <p>Three years ago, Daniel moved to Canada from Brazil with only two suitcases and a small amount of savings. He didn't know anyone in his new city, and his English was just good enough to order coffee and ask for directions. During his first few months, he struggled to find work; many companies wanted "Canadian experience," which he didn't have yet. Eventually, a small logistics company gave him a chance as a warehouse assistant, and he promised himself he would learn something new every single day.</p>
        <p>At first, understanding his coworkers was exhausting. People spoke quickly, used slang, and laughed at jokes he didn't understand. Daniel started writing down new expressions in a notebook and asking his coworkers to explain them during breaks. Slowly, conversations became easier. He joined a weekend soccer league, where he met people from all over the world, and two of his teammates became close friends.</p>
        <p>Today, Daniel has been promoted to shift supervisor, and he often helps train new employees who remind him of himself three years ago. He still makes mistakes in English, but he isn't afraid of them anymore. When people ask if he misses Brazil, he says yes — but he also says that Canada finally feels like home.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:14px;">Multiple Choice</h3>
      <div class="q"><span class="q-num">1.</span><span class="q-prompt">What did Daniel bring with him when he first arrived in Canada?</span>
        <div class="choices">
          <div class="choice"><span class="letter">A</span>A car and a laptop</div>
          <div class="choice"><span class="letter">B</span>Two suitcases and some savings</div>
          <div class="choice"><span class="letter">C</span>A job offer letter</div>
          <div class="choice"><span class="letter">D</span>His family</div>
        </div></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="q-num">2.</span><span class="q-prompt">What was one of the biggest challenges Daniel faced when looking for work?</span>
        <div class="choices">
